[00:00.79]Lesson 16 | 第16课
[00:02.51]The modern city | 现代城市
[00:09.50]What is the author's main argument about the modern city? | 关于现代城市，作者的主要论点是什么？
[00:15.45]In the organization of industrial life the influence of the factory upon the physiological and mental state of the workers has been completely neglected. | 在工业生活的组织当中，工厂对工人生理和心理状态的影响完全被忽视了。
[00:26.73]Modern industry is based on the conception of the maximum production at lowest cost, | 现代工业的基本概念是：以最低成本获取最大产量，
[00:33.05]in order that an individual or a group of individuals may earn as much money as possible. | 以便个人或集团能赚到尽可能多的钱。
[00:40.09]It has expanded without any idea of the true nature of the human beings who run the machines, | 工业的发展毫无考虑机器操作者的真正人性，
[00:46.55]and without giving any consideration to the effects produced on the individuals and on their descendants by the artificial mode of existence imposed by the factory. | 也毫无考虑工厂强加于人的那种人为生存方式对个人及其后代所产生的影响。
[00:58.63]The great cities have been built with no regard for us. | 大城市的建设毫不顾及我们。
[01:02.65]The shape and dimensions of the skyscrapers depend entirely on the necessity of obtaining the maximum income per square foot of ground, | 摩天大楼的形状和大小完全取决于获得每平方英尺土地最大收入的必要性，
[01:11.68]and of offering to the tenants offices and apartments that please them. | 以及向租户提供使他们满意的办公室和住房。
[01:16.53]This caused the construction of gigantic buildings where too large masses of human beings are crowded together. | 这就造成了巨大建筑物的建造，过多的人群挤在一起。
[01:24.66]Civilized men like such a way of living. | 文明人喜欢这样的生活方式。
[01:27.97]While they enjoy the comfort and banal luxury of their dwelling, they do not realize that they are deprived of the necessities of life. | 当他们享受着住宅的舒适和庸俗的奢华时，他们并没有意识到他们被剥夺了生活必需品。
[01:37.06]The modern city consists of monstrous edifices and of dark, narrow streets full of petrol fumes and toxic gases, | 现代城市由怪兽般的高楼大厦和充斥着汽油味和毒气的黑暗狭窄街道组成，
[01:46.20]torn by the noise of the taxicabs, lorries and buses, and thronged ceaselessly by great crowds. | 出租汽车、卡车和公共汽车的噪声撕裂着它，大群的人流不断在其中熙来攘往。
[01:54.58]Obviously, it has not been planned for the good of its inhabitants. | 显然，现代城市的规划并没有为居民的利益着想。
